## Entry for the Table of Contents
A series of single-atom metal implanted N-doped carbon (namely $M_{1}$ -N-C; $\mathsf{M}=\mathsf{F}\mathsf{e}$ , Co, Ni and Cu), with almost identical carbon support environment, are constructed based on multivariate MOFs. These $M_{1}$ -N-C model catalysts make it possible to discern activity difference of diverse single-atom metal species toward $\mathsf{C O}_{2}$ electroreduction. Significantly, the best-performed $N i_{1}-N-C$ is able to achieve highly selective reduction of $\mathsf{C O}_{2}$ even at low pressures.
